[medium] `diskStatusChange` should get internal linkage — put it in an anonymous namespace or mark it `static` — so it stays scoped to this translation unit and can't trigger ODR issues. Marking it `constexpr` would also allow compile-time evaluation.

Suggested approach:
```cpp
namespace
{
    constexpr int diskStatusChange(bool old_val, bool new_val)
    {
        return static_cast<int>(new_val) - static_cast<int>(old_val);
    }
}
```
Or simply:
```cpp
static constexpr int diskStatusChange(bool old_val, bool new_val)
{
    return static_cast<int>(new_val) - static_cast<int>(old_val);
}
```
